- op: discuss  # 0c2d
  at: '2026-05-30T09:06:43Z'  # 0c2d
  by: agent  # 0c2d
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 0c2d
  clock: 3  # 0c2d
  nonce: 0c2d  # 0c2d
  message: "Cross-ref backfill (2026-05-30, deeper-issue investigation): shares the \"output format assumes a smaller dataset than reality delivers\" mechanic with INV-modor (sketch_precomputed.readme_description truncated at 207 chars mid-sentence). Both surface the absence of a data-aware display contract — neither cli.py:3608-3621 (symbols numeric columns) nor the README extractor passes the data's actual range/length distribution to its formatter. Code reference confirmed: In/Out/Deg columns at cli.py:3614-3616 have no min_width; only Kind at 3613 uses a data-driven width. Suggest the structural fix is to compute min_width per numeric column from max(int) digit-count before Rich rendering."  # 0c2d
- op: discuss  # 0545
  at: '2026-06-02T07:09:29Z'  # 0545
  by: agent  # 0545
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 0545
  clock: 4  # 0545
  nonce: '0545'  # 0545
  message: "Pass-30 face: `symbols` subcommand silently filters node kinds (F30.11).\n\nINV-ripoh's existing scope is \"symbols Deg column truncates 4-digit centrality values on default terminal\" — column-truncation face. Pass-30 finds a second `symbols`-subcommand issue with the same root cause family (consumer-facing display contract diverges from substrate completeness).\n\n**Observation.** `hypergumbo symbols --input /tmp/hg-dogfood-s21/bm.json --limit 20` reports:\n> \"31620 additional symbols omitted for brevity; run with --all to show them\"\n\nTotal claimed = 20 shown + 31620 = **31640 symbols**. Substrate has **34253 nodes**. Delta = **2613 silently excluded** (7.6% of substrate). With `--all`, output line count confirms the 31640 cap.\n\nExcluded kinds: `--kind file` (substrate has 901 file nodes) returns **\"No symbols found\"**. `--kind variable` (substrate has 1609 variable nodes) returns **\"No symbols found\"**. `--kind call_site` (130 nodes) returns 130 correctly. So `symbols` subcommand silently excludes file (901) + variable (1609) + ~103 other low-count kinds = ~2613 nodes.\n\nThe CLI's `--all` flag's contract is not consistent with the noun \"symbols\": it shows all call-graph-participating symbols but not all substrate Symbol records. File-kind and variable-kind Symbols exist in substrate but are invisible to the CLI even with explicit `--kind` request and `--all`.\n\n**Severity.** Consumer impact is medium — users searching for a known file name via `symbols` will get \"No symbols found\" and conclude the file isn't in the substrate, when in fact it's there but the subcommand filtered it. The `--kind file` empty response is the worst failure mode because it's actively misleading (the user asked specifically for files and got \"none exist\").\n\n**Fix-path candidates.**\n- Disclose the filter in `--help` (\"symbols subcommand reports function/method/class/external_symbol/etc. — file and variable kinds are excluded; use `routes` or direct bm.json query for file-level info\").\n- Add a header note when `--kind file` or `--kind variable` is requested explicitly, saying \"this kind is excluded from `symbols`; see `<subcommand>` for `<kind>` queries.\"\n- Or relax the filter to include all substrate kinds and add a `--exclude-kind file,variable` flag for the current behavior.\n\nSame root pattern as INV-rarol (\"Explanation subcommand output does not deliver its documented contract\") at a different subcommand surface. Could also fold under INV-ripoh as a sibling face (both surface `symbols` display contract gaps). Filed here as INV-ripoh discussion entry to keep scope cohesive; consider a peer WI if/when the column-truncation fix lands and this face needs independent tracking.\n\nNo status change. Pass-30 supplies the second `symbols`-subcommand display-contract gap.\n\nProbe artifact: pass-30 probe 3 CLI testing — outputs at /tmp/pass30_cli_symbols.log + /tmp/pass30_cli_symbols_all.log."  # 0545
- op: discuss  # b631
  at: '2026-06-02T07:32:56Z'  # b631
  by: agent  # b631
  actor: jgstern_agent  # b631
  clock: 5  # b631
  nonce: b631  # b631
  message: "Pass-31 face: column-truncation extends from Deg column to In column on `symbols --all` (F31.1).\n\nINV-ripoh's title is \"symbols Deg column truncates 4-digit centrality values on default terminal\". Pass-31 finds the In column has the same problem at the same column width.\n\n**Observation.** `hypergumbo symbols --input /tmp/hg-dogfood-s21/bm.json --all` row for Edge.create:\n```\nEdge.create  method   …  0  …  packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/ir.py\n```\n\n- substrate ground truth: in_deg = 557, out_deg = 0\n- `In` column shows `…` (truncated — 557 doesn't fit)\n- `Out` column shows `0` (1-digit fits)\n- `Deg` column shows `…` (truncated — 557 doesn't fit)\n\nThe column widths in the default rendering are insufficient for 3-4-digit connectivity values. Both `In` and `Deg` truncate. `Out` fits because most symbols have small out-degree.\n\nFor pass-30 F30.12 confirmation: `register_analyzer` has in_deg=315 and displays correctly in some rows but truncates in others depending on layout — the per-row `Deg` value (sum of In+Out) blows past the column width for high-in-degree symbols. Edge.create is the worst case in the substrate (557 in-deg).\n\nSame root cause as INV-ripoh's existing scope (column width insufficient); pass-31 extends to the second column (In) with the same problem. Workaround `--col-width 1000` exists per `symbols --help` but the default rendering produces actively misleading output for connectivity-heavy symbols.\n\nFix-path candidate: per-column width auto-sizing based on the maximum value in the column for the rendered rows. Default rendering would adapt to the substrate's connectivity distribution.\n\nNo status change. Pass-31 supplies the second instance — In column truncation alongside the catalogued Deg column truncation — making the column-width issue a 2-column problem rather than 1-column.\n\nProbe artifact: pass-31 probe A.3 — `hypergumbo explain Edge.create` showed 557 in-degree correctly; the same symbol's `symbols` row showed `…  0  …` truncated."  # b631
- op: discuss  # 7027
  at: '2026-06-02T17:13:16Z'  # 7027
  by: agent  # 7027
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7027
  clock: 6  # 7027
  nonce: '7027'  # 7027
  message: "Pass-34 F34.D1 — `hypergumbo search` silently filters `external_symbol` kind from results.\n\nTested 10 patterns against case-insensitive substring on `node.name` in `/tmp/hg-dogfood-s21/bm.json`, compared against `hypergumbo search PATTERN --limit 100000` header counts:\n- `parse`: substrate=571 vs search=545 (delta=26)\n- `test_`: substrate=20372 vs search=20368 (delta=4)\n- `analyze`: substrate=2566 vs search=2530 (delta=36)\n\nProbe D2 root-caused the delta by grouping search output records by kind: `{function:159, method:335, class:38, variable:2, call_site:9, file:2}`. Substrate grouping shows the same kinds plus `external_symbol:26`. **The delta of 26 matches exactly the external_symbol count.**\n\nVerified the filter is kind-based by running `search parse --kind call_site --limit 5` which DOES return call_site nodes — so search supports the kind filter, it just default-excludes external_symbol when no --kind is specified. No override; no `--include-externals` flag.\n\nThis is the same finding-family as F30.11 (INV-ripoh scope already): `symbols` subcommand silently filters file (901) + variable (1609) kinds. Pass-34 extends to `search` filtering `external_symbol`. Three subcommands now exhibit the silent-kind-filter pattern:\n- `symbols` (default): filters file, variable\n- `symbols --all`: filters 2613 nodes (per F30.11)\n- `search` (default): filters external_symbol\n\nThe three filters use different kind-exclusion sets with no documented rationale. INV-ripoh's \"display-contract gap\" framing extends from the column-truncation face (the original title) to the silent-kind-filter face (F30.11) to the search-kind-filter face (F34.D1).\n\n**Fix-path candidate.** Document each subcommand's default-excluded kinds in --help text; provide a flag (e.g., `--include-all-kinds`) to override; emit a footer line \"N additional symbols matched but filtered (excluded kinds: external_symbol)\" when filter activates.\n\n**Probe artifact:** `/tmp/p34_probeD.py`, `/tmp/p34_probeD2.py`, `/tmp/p34_outputD.log`, `/tmp/p34_outputD2.log`. No status change."  # 7027
